  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "epan: register_tap_listener could cause double free on error",
  "description": "register_tap_listener has various paths where an error string can be\nreturned, indicating an error while setting up the tap listener. In\none of the paths, where the display filter is processed, a call is made\nto free_tap_listener to release all of the tap listener structure.\nIncluded in this is an attempt to call the tap.finish callback.\n\nThis has two problems associated with it. A calling function can not\nassume the tap.finish callback has been called on error, since not all\nerror paths make this call. Due to this fact non of the callers of\nregister_tap_listener make this assumption, on error they perform\ncleanup operations themselves. This could cause double free errors.\n\nSecondly, since the tap listener struct has not been setup completely\nwhen free_tap_listener is called in the error path, the call to the\ntap.finish callback is never made. This is what the comment is about.\n\nAs a matter of fact non of the tap listener struct parts on which\nfree_tap_listener operates has been setup yet, apart from the struct\nitself. Therefore the whole call to free_tap_listener in this error\npath is not better than simply freeing the tap listener struct itself.\n\nTherefor, to simplify the code and avoid any future double free errors,\nswap the use of free_tap_listener by a simple free of the struct.",
